"""Cybersecurity glossary, part 13: fraud, money movement, online abuse and the criminal ecosystem. Protective descriptions only. fr/rw/sw are drafts for fluent review."""
from cyber_terms_12 import T

TERMS_13 = [
    T("money-laundering", "Money laundering", ["money laundering", "laundering", "blanchiment d'argent", "kuvanga amafaranga y'inyibano", "utakatishaji fedha"], "governance", "bank vault and cash", {"fr": "Blanchiment d'argent", "sw": "Utakatishaji fedha", "rw": "Kuvunjisha amafaranga y'inyibano"},
      ("Hiding the criminal origin of money (from fraud, ransomware or theft) by moving it through many accounts, businesses or crypto wallets until it looks legitimate.", "Banks use KYC and monitoring to spot it. Never let anyone use your account or mobile-money number to “receive and forward” money: you can become a money mule and be held responsible."),
      ("Dissimuler l'origine criminelle d'argent (fraude, rançongiciel, vol) en le faisant passer par de nombreux comptes, entreprises ou portefeuilles crypto jusqu'à ce qu'il paraisse légitime.", "Les banques utilisent le KYC et la surveillance pour le repérer. Ne laissez jamais personne utiliser votre compte ou numéro mobile money pour « recevoir et transférer » : vous pourriez devenir une mule et être tenu responsable."),
      ("Guhisha inkomoko mbi y'amafaranga (aturuka ku buriganya, ransomware cyangwa ubujura) bayanyuza ku makonti, ibigo cyangwa wallet nyinshi kugeza asa n'ayemewe.", "Amabanki akoresha KYC no gukurikirana kugira ngo ayibone. Ntukemere ko umuntu akoresha konti yawe cyangwa nimero ya mobile money «yakira akohereza» amafaranga: wahinduka mule ukabibazwa."),
      ("Kuficha asili ya uhalifu ya pesa (kutoka ulaghai, ransomware au wizi) kwa kuzipitisha kwenye akaunti, biashara au pochi za crypto nyingi hadi zionekane halali.", "Benki hutumia KYC na ufuatiliaji kuigundua. Kamwe usimruhusu mtu kutumia akaunti au namba yako ya pesa za simu «kupokea na kutuma» pesa: unaweza kuwa mule na kuwajibishwa.")),
    T("money-mule", "Money mule", ["money mule", "mule account", "money muling", "mule", "receive and forward money"], "attacks", "bank transfer", {"fr": "Mule financière", "sw": "Money mule", "rw": "Mule y'amafaranga"},
      ("A person whose bank or mobile-money account is used (knowingly or not) to receive and pass on stolen money for criminals. Recruiters promise an easy job or commission.", "Warning signs: a job that only asks you to move money, offers a percentage, or a stranger who “accidentally” pays you. Refuse, report, and keep records. Being a mule can lead to arrest and a closed account."),
      ("Personne dont le compte bancaire ou mobile money sert (sciemment ou non) à recevoir et faire suivre de l'argent volé pour des criminels. Les recruteurs promettent un travail facile ou une commission.", "Signes : un emploi qui consiste seulement à déplacer de l'argent, offre un pourcentage, ou un inconnu qui vous paie « par erreur ». Refusez, signalez et gardez les preuves. Être mule peut mener à l'arrestation et à la fermeture du compte."),
      ("Umuntu konti ye ya banki cyangwa mobile money ikoreshwa (abizi cyangwa atabizi) mu kwakira no kohereza amafaranga yibwe y'abagizi ba nabi. Abamushaka bamusezeranya akazi koroshye cyangwa komisiyo.", "Ibimenyetso: akazi gusaba kwimura amafaranga gusa, kagutanga ijanisha, cyangwa umuntu utazi ukwishyura «kubw'impanuka». Hakana, ubimenyeshe kandi ubike ibimenyetso. Kuba mule bishobora gutera gufungwa no gufungirwa konti."),
      ("Mtu ambaye akaunti yake ya benki au pesa za simu hutumiwa (kwa kujua au bila kujua) kupokea na kupitisha pesa zilizoibwa kwa wahalifu. Waajiri huahidi kazi rahisi au kamisheni.", "Dalili: kazi inayohitaji kuhamisha pesa tu, inayotoa asilimia, au mgeni anayekulipa «kwa makosa». Kataa, ripoti na uhifadhi ushahidi. Kuwa mule kunaweza kusababisha kukamatwa na akaunti kufungwa.")),
    T("carding", "Carding", ["carding", "card fraud", "stolen card numbers", "card dumps", "cvv shop"], "attacks", "credit cards", {"fr": "Carding (fraude à la carte)", "sw": "Carding", "rw": "Carding"},
      ("Trading and using stolen bank card details, usually bought on criminal marketplaces, to make purchases or cash out.", "Protect yourself: shop on trusted sites, use virtual or single-use cards, enable transaction alerts, check statements and report any unknown charge to the bank immediately."),
      ("Le commerce et l'utilisation de données de cartes bancaires volées, souvent achetées sur des marchés criminels, pour acheter ou retirer de l'argent.", "Protégez-vous : achetez sur des sites de confiance, utilisez des cartes virtuelles ou à usage unique, activez les alertes de transaction, vérifiez vos relevés et signalez toute opération inconnue à la banque sans délai."),
      ("Gucuruza no gukoresha amakuru y'amakarita ya banki yibwe, akenshi agurwa ku masoko y'abagizi ba nabi, kugura cyangwa gukuramo amafaranga.", "Wirinde: gura ku mbuga zizewe, koresha amakarita ya virtual cyangwa akoreshwa rimwe, fungura ubutumwa bw'ibikorwa, reba raporo za banki kandi umenyeshe banki vuba igikorwa utazi."),
      ("Kuuza na kutumia taarifa za kadi za benki zilizoibwa, mara nyingi hununuliwa kwenye masoko ya wahalifu, kununua au kutoa pesa.", "Jilinde: nunua kwenye tovuti zinazoaminika, tumia kadi pepe au za matumizi moja, washa tahadhari za miamala, kagua taarifa na ripoti malipo yasiyojulikana kwa benki mara moja.")),
    T("card-testing", "Card testing", ["card testing", "bin attack", "carding bot", "small test payments"], "attacks", "online payment form", {"fr": "Test de cartes (card testing)", "sw": "Card testing", "rw": "Card testing"},
      ("Criminals use bots to try many small payments on a shop's checkout to find which stolen card numbers still work, before using them for large purchases.", "Shops defend with CAPTCHA, rate limiting, fraud scoring and 3-D Secure. Cardholders who see tiny unknown charges should report them at once: they often come before bigger fraud."),
      ("Les criminels utilisent des robots pour tenter de nombreux petits paiements sur la caisse d'une boutique afin de trouver quels numéros de cartes volées fonctionnent encore, avant de gros achats.", "Les boutiques se défendent avec CAPTCHA, limitation de débit, score de fraude et 3-D Secure. Les porteurs voyant de minuscules débits inconnus doivent les signaler tout de suite : ils précèdent souvent une fraude plus grosse."),
      ("Abagizi ba nabi bakoresha bots mu kugerageza ubwishyu bwinshi buto ku iduka rya interineti kugira ngo bamenye nimero z'amakarita yibwe zigikora, mbere yo kugura byinshi.", "Amaduka arinda akoresheje CAPTCHA, rate limiting, isuzuma ry'uburiganya na 3-D Secure. Abafite amakarita babonye amafaranga mato batazi bagomba kubimenyesha vuba: akenshi biza mbere y'uburiganya bukomeye."),
      ("Wahalifu hutumia bots kujaribu malipo mengi madogo kwenye malipo ya duka ili kujua namba za kadi zilizoibwa zinazofanya kazi, kabla ya manunuzi makubwa.", "Maduka hujilinda kwa CAPTCHA, kikomo cha maombi, alama ya ulaghai na 3-D Secure. Wenye kadi wanaoona makato madogo yasiyojulikana waripoti mara moja: mara nyingi hutangulia ulaghai mkubwa.")),
    T("chargeback-fraud", "Chargeback fraud", ["chargeback fraud", "friendly fraud", "false chargeback", "refund abuse"], "attacks", "online payment dispute", {"fr": "Fraude au rejet de débit", "sw": "Ulaghai wa chargeback", "rw": "Uburiganya bwa chargeback"},
      ("Abusing the card-dispute system: a buyer receives goods or services, then tells the bank the payment was unauthorised and gets the money back (also called friendly fraud).", "Sellers keep proof of delivery, clear descriptions and signed receipts and use fraud tools. Buyers should know that false disputes are fraud and can lead to account bans or legal action."),
      ("Abus du système de contestation de paiement par carte : l'acheteur reçoit le bien ou service, puis déclare à la banque que le paiement n'était pas autorisé et se fait rembourser (aussi appelé fraude amicale).", "Les vendeurs conservent preuves de livraison, descriptions claires et reçus signés et utilisent des outils anti-fraude. Les acheteurs doivent savoir qu'une fausse contestation est une fraude pouvant entraîner bannissement ou poursuites."),
      ("Gukoresha nabi uburyo bwo kujuririra ubwishyu bwa karita: umuguzi yakira ibicuruzwa cyangwa serivisi, hanyuma abwira banki ko ubwishyu butemewe agasubizwa amafaranga (bita friendly fraud).", "Abacuruzi babika ibimenyetso by'itangwa, ibisobanuro bisobanutse n'inyemezabwishyu zasinywe kandi bagakoresha ibikoresho birwanya uburiganya. Abaguzi bamenye ko kujuririra mu binyoma ari uburiganya bushobora gutera guhagarikwa cyangwa gukurikiranwa."),
      ("Matumizi mabaya ya mfumo wa migogoro ya malipo ya kadi: mnunuzi hupokea bidhaa au huduma, kisha huiambia benki malipo hayakuidhinishwa na kurejeshewa pesa (pia huitwa friendly fraud).", "Wauzaji hutunza ushahidi wa uwasilishaji, maelezo wazi na risiti zilizosainiwa na kutumia zana za kuzuia ulaghai. Wanunuzi wajue migogoro ya uongo ni ulaghai unaoweza kusababisha kupigwa marufuku au kushtakiwa.")),
    T("invoice-redirection", "Invoice redirection fraud", ["invoice redirection", "payment diversion", "vendor email compromise", "changed bank details scam", "supplier bank change fraud"], "attacks", "invoice and bank details", {"fr": "Fraude au changement de RIB", "sw": "Ulaghai wa kubadili akaunti ya malipo", "rw": "Uburiganya bwo guhindura konti yo kwishyura"},
      ("A criminal, often inside a hacked or spoofed email thread, tells a company that a supplier's bank details have changed, so the next payment goes to the criminal's account.", "Always confirm any change of payment details by calling a number you already have, never one from the email. Require two people to approve changes and new accounts, and check names match."),
      ("Un criminel, souvent dans un fil d'e-mails piraté ou usurpé, annonce à une entreprise que les coordonnées bancaires d'un fournisseur ont changé, et le prochain paiement part sur son compte.", "Confirmez toujours tout changement de coordonnées par un numéro que vous possédez déjà, jamais celui de l'e-mail. Exigez deux validations pour les changements et nouveaux comptes, et vérifiez que les noms correspondent."),
      ("Umugizi wa nabi, akenshi mu mwandiko w'imeri wibwe cyangwa wiganwe, abwira ikigo ko konti ya banki y'utanga ibicuruzwa yahindutse, ubwishyu bukurikira bukajya kuri konti ye.", "Buri gihe emeza ihindura ry'amakuru yo kwishyura uhamagara nimero usanzwe ufite, si iyo mu imeri. Saba abantu babiri bemeze ihindura n'amakonti mashya kandi urebe ko amazina ahura."),
      ("Mhalifu, mara nyingi ndani ya mazungumzo ya barua pepe yaliyodukuliwa au kughushiwa, huambia kampuni kuwa akaunti ya benki ya muuzaji imebadilika, hivyo malipo yajayo huenda kwa akaunti yake.", "Thibitisha kila mabadiliko ya taarifa za malipo kwa kupiga namba unayoijua tayari, kamwe si ya barua pepe. Hitaji watu wawili kuidhinisha mabadiliko na akaunti mpya na hakikisha majina yanalingana.")),
    T("synthetic-identity", "Synthetic identity fraud", ["synthetic identity", "synthetic identity fraud", "fake identity creation", "fabricated identity"], "attacks", "identity documents", {"fr": "Fraude à l'identité synthétique", "sw": "Utambulisho wa kubuni", "rw": "Umwirondoro w'ibihimbano"},
      ("Building a fake person by mixing real data (such as a stolen national ID number) with invented details, then using it to open accounts and borrow money.", "Hard to see because no single real person complains at first. Protect your ID number, check your credit and account records, and let institutions verify identity with several independent checks."),
      ("Fabriquer une fausse personne en mélangeant de vraies données (comme un numéro d'identité volé) et des détails inventés, puis l'utiliser pour ouvrir des comptes et emprunter de l'argent.", "Difficile à voir car aucune vraie personne ne se plaint au début. Protégez votre numéro d'identité, vérifiez vos dossiers de crédit et de comptes, et faites vérifier l'identité par plusieurs contrôles indépendants."),
      ("Guhimba umuntu uvanga amakuru nyakuri (nk'inomero y'irangamuntu yibwe) n'ibyahimbwe, hanyuma ukayikoresha mu gufungura konti no kuguza amafaranga.", "Biragoye kubibona kuko nta muntu nyawe ubanza kubirega. Rinda nimero y'irangamuntu yawe, reba inyandiko z'inguzanyo na konti kandi ibigo bigenzure umwirondoro mu buryo bwinshi bwigenga."),
      ("Kujenga mtu bandia kwa kuchanganya data halisi (kama namba ya kitambulisho iliyoibwa) na maelezo ya kubuni, kisha kuitumia kufungua akaunti na kukopa pesa.", "Ni vigumu kuona kwa sababu hakuna mtu halisi analalamika mwanzoni. Linda namba yako ya kitambulisho, kagua rekodi zako za mikopo na akaunti, na taasisi zihakiki utambulisho kwa ukaguzi kadhaa huru.")),
    T("click-and-ad-fraud", "Click fraud and ad fraud", ["click fraud", "ad fraud", "fake clicks", "invalid traffic", "affiliate fraud"], "attacks", "online advertising", {"fr": "Fraude au clic et publicitaire", "sw": "Ulaghai wa kubofya na matangazo", "rw": "Uburiganya bw'ibyo gukanda n'amamaza"},
      ("Generating fake clicks, views or installs (often with bots or infected devices) to steal advertising money or to drain a competitor's ad budget.", "Advertisers use traffic verification, fraud detection and limits on suspicious sources. Ordinary users: infected devices can be secretly used for this, so keep phones and PCs clean and updated."),
      ("Générer de faux clics, vues ou installations (souvent avec des robots ou des appareils infectés) pour voler de l'argent publicitaire ou épuiser le budget d'un concurrent.", "Les annonceurs utilisent la vérification du trafic, la détection de fraude et des limites sur les sources suspectes. Utilisateurs : des appareils infectés peuvent servir à cela en secret, gardez téléphones et PC propres et à jour."),
      ("Gukora gukanda, kureba cyangwa gushyiraho porogaramu bitari ukuri (akenshi hakoreshwa bots cyangwa ibikoresho byanduye) kugira ngo biyibe amafaranga y'amamaza cyangwa bamareho ingengo y'umunywanyi.", "Abamamaza bakoresha kugenzura urujya n'uruza, gutahura uburiganya no kugabanya inkomoko zikekwa. Abakoresha basanzwe: ibikoresho byanduye bishobora gukoreshwa rwihishwa, bisukure kandi ubivugurure."),
      ("Kuunda mibofyo, maoni au usakinishaji bandia (mara nyingi kwa bots au vifaa vilivyoambukizwa) kuiba pesa za matangazo au kumaliza bajeti ya mshindani.", "Watangazaji hutumia uhakiki wa trafiki, kugundua ulaghai na vikwazo kwa vyanzo vinavyotiliwa shaka. Watumiaji: vifaa vilivyoambukizwa vinaweza kutumiwa kimya kimya, viweke safi na vilivyosasishwa.")),
    T("swatting", "Swatting", ["swatting", "fake emergency report", "hoax police call"], "attacks", "emergency phone call", {"fr": "Swatting (faux appel d'urgence)", "sw": "Swatting", "rw": "Swatting"},
      ("A malicious hoax where someone falsely reports a serious emergency at a victim's address to send armed police there, often after doxxing the victim.", "It is a crime that can cause injury or death. Protect your home address (do not share it, remove it from data-broker sites) and report threats. Anyone who makes a false emergency report can be prosecuted."),
      ("Un canular malveillant où quelqu'un signale à tort une urgence grave à l'adresse d'une victime pour y envoyer la police armée, souvent après avoir divulgué ses informations (doxxing).", "C'est un délit qui peut causer des blessures ou la mort. Protégez votre adresse (ne la partagez pas, retirez-la des sites de courtiers de données) et signalez les menaces. Un faux signalement d'urgence est passible de poursuites."),
      ("Ibinyoma bigamije kugirira nabi aho umuntu avuga ko hari ibyago bikomeye ku rugo rw'uwo yibasiye kugira ngo polisi ifite intwaro ijyeyo, akenshi nyuma yo gutangaza amakuru ye (doxxing).", "Ni icyaha gishobora gutera gukomereka cyangwa urupfu. Rinda aderesi y'iwawe (ntuyisangize, uyikure ku mbuga zicuruza amakuru) kandi ubimenyeshe iyo wibasiwe. Gutanga raporo y'ibyago y'ibinyoma birakurikiranwa."),
      ("Utani wa kudhuru ambapo mtu huripoti kwa uongo dharura kubwa kwenye anwani ya mwathirika ili polisi wenye silaha waende huko, mara nyingi baada ya kufichua taarifa zake (doxxing).", "Ni kosa la jinai linaloweza kusababisha jeraha au kifo. Linda anwani ya nyumbani (usiishiriki, iondoe kwenye tovuti za wauzaji data) na ripoti vitisho. Kutoa ripoti ya dharura ya uongo huchukuliwa hatua za kisheria.")),
    T("online-grooming", "Online grooming", ["online grooming", "grooming", "child grooming", "online predators", "predator"], "social", "child using a tablet", {"fr": "Pédopiégeage (grooming)", "sw": "Grooming mtandaoni", "rw": "Grooming kuri interineti"},
      ("When an adult builds trust with a child online (often pretending to be a friend or peer) in order to exploit or abuse them. It is a serious crime.", "Parents and teachers: talk openly, know the apps children use, set privacy controls and teach them never to keep secrets with online “friends” or send images. If a child is at risk, report to the police or a child-protection service."),
      ("Quand un adulte gagne la confiance d'un enfant en ligne (souvent en se faisant passer pour un ami ou un camarade) afin de l'exploiter ou d'abuser de lui. C'est un crime grave.", "Parents et enseignants : parlez ouvertement, connaissez les applications utilisées, réglez la confidentialité et apprenez aux enfants à ne jamais garder de secrets avec des « amis » en ligne ni envoyer d'images. En cas de risque, signalez à la police ou à un service de protection de l'enfance."),
      ("Iyo umuntu mukuru yubaka icyizere n'umwana kuri interineti (akenshi yiyoberanya incuti cyangwa mugenzi) kugira ngo amukoreshe nabi cyangwa amusambanye. Ni icyaha gikomeye.", "Ababyeyi n'abarimu: muganire mu mucyo, mumenye porogaramu abana bakoresha, mushyireho ibanga ry'amakuru kandi mwigishe abana kudahisha ibanga n'«incuti» zo kuri interineti cyangwa kohereza amafoto. Umwana ari mu kaga, bimenyeshe polisi cyangwa urwego rurengera abana."),
      ("Wakati mtu mzima anapojenga imani na mtoto mtandaoni (mara nyingi akijifanya rafiki au mwenzake) ili amnyonye au kumdhulumu. Ni kosa kubwa la jinai.", "Wazazi na walimu: zungumza wazi, jua programu watoto wanazotumia, weka faragha na wafundishe kamwe kutoficha siri na «marafiki» wa mtandaoni wala kutuma picha. Mtoto akiwa hatarini, ripoti polisi au huduma ya ulinzi wa watoto.")),
    T("image-based-abuse", "Image-based abuse", ["image-based abuse", "revenge porn", "non-consensual intimate images", "intimate image abuse", "nudes leak"], "social", "phone with privacy lock", {"fr": "Abus d'images intimes", "sw": "Unyanyasaji wa picha za faragha", "rw": "Gukoresha nabi amafoto y'ibanga"},
      ("Sharing or threatening to share someone's private or intimate images without consent, including fake (AI-made) images. It is a form of abuse and in many places a crime.", "If it happens to you: do not pay or negotiate, save evidence (screenshots, links), report to the platform and the police, and seek support. Never forward such images: sharing them is itself harmful and may be illegal."),
      ("Partager ou menacer de partager des images privées ou intimes de quelqu'un sans son consentement, y compris des images truquées (créées par IA). C'est une forme d'abus et, dans beaucoup d'endroits, un délit.", "Si cela vous arrive : ne payez pas et ne négociez pas, conservez les preuves (captures, liens), signalez à la plateforme et à la police et cherchez du soutien. Ne transférez jamais ces images : les partager est nuisible et peut être illégal."),
      ("Gusangiza cyangwa gutera ubwoba ko uzasangiza amafoto y'ibanga cyangwa y'umubiri wa muntu nta ruhushya, harimo n'ay'ibihimbano (yakozwe na AI). Ni uburyo bwo guhohotera kandi mu bice byinshi ni icyaha.", "Bikubayeho: ntukishyure cyangwa ngo uganire, bika ibimenyetso (screenshots, amahuza), umenyeshe urubuga na polisi kandi ushake ubufasha. Ntuzigere wohereza ayo mafoto: kuyasangiza byonyine ni ukugirira nabi kandi bishobora kuba icyaha."),
      ("Kushiriki au kutishia kushiriki picha za faragha za mtu bila ridhaa, ikiwemo picha bandia (zilizotengenezwa na AI). Ni aina ya unyanyasaji na mahali pengi ni kosa la jinai.", "Ukikutwa nayo: usilipe wala kujadiliana, hifadhi ushahidi (picha za skrini, viungo), ripoti kwa jukwaa na polisi na utafute msaada. Kamwe usitume picha hizo: kuzishiriki ni kudhuru na kunaweza kuwa kosa.")),
    T("data-broker", "Data broker", ["data broker", "data brokers", "people search site", "data aggregator", "opt out of data brokers"], "privacy", "database of personal information", {"fr": "Courtier de données", "sw": "Dalali wa data", "rw": "Umucuruzi w'amakuru bwite"},
      ("A company that collects personal information from many sources (public records, apps, purchases) and sells or shares profiles about people, often without their direct knowledge.", "Reduce exposure: limit what you share, review app permissions, use opt-out tools where they exist and use different emails or numbers for different services. Criminals can use broker data for scams and stalking."),
      ("Entreprise qui collecte des informations personnelles de nombreuses sources (registres publics, applications, achats) et vend ou partage des profils, souvent à l'insu des personnes.", "Réduisez l'exposition : limitez ce que vous partagez, vérifiez les permissions des applications, utilisez les outils de retrait quand ils existent et des e-mails ou numéros différents selon les services. Les criminels peuvent utiliser ces données pour arnaques et harcèlement."),
      ("Ikigo gikusanya amakuru bwite mu masoko menshi (inyandiko rusange, porogaramu, ibyo wagurishije) kikayagurisha cyangwa kikayasangiza, akenshi nta ruhushya rw'abo avugwaho.", "Gabanya ibyo ugaragaza: gabanya ibyo usangiza, reba uburenganzira bwa porogaramu, koresha uburyo bwo kwikura ku rutonde aho buhari kandi ukoreshe imeri cyangwa nimero zitandukanye kuri serivisi zitandukanye. Abagizi ba nabi bashobora gukoresha ayo makuru mu buriganya no gukurikirana."),
      ("Kampuni inayokusanya taarifa binafsi kutoka vyanzo vingi (rekodi za umma, programu, manunuzi) na kuuza au kushiriki wasifu wa watu, mara nyingi bila wao kujua.", "Punguza mfichuo: punguza unachoshiriki, kagua ruhusa za programu, tumia zana za kujiondoa pale zinapopatikana na utumie barua pepe au namba tofauti kwa huduma tofauti. Wahalifu wanaweza kutumia data hiyo kwa ulaghai na kufuatilia.")),
    T("stealer-logs", "Stealer logs", ["stealer logs", "infostealer logs", "stolen credentials logs", "redline logs", "stealer log"], "malware", "stolen data archive", {"fr": "Journaux de vol (stealer logs)", "sw": "Stealer logs", "rw": "Stealer logs"},
      ("Bundles of passwords, cookies, saved cards and other data that infostealer malware secretly copies from infected devices and that criminals then sell or share.", "If a device may have been infected, change passwords from a clean device, sign out all sessions, enable MFA and remove the malware. Do not download cracked software or pirated games, the common source of infostealers."),
      ("Lots de mots de passe, cookies, cartes enregistrées et autres données que des infostealers copient en secret depuis des appareils infectés et que des criminels vendent ou partagent.", "Si un appareil a pu être infecté, changez vos mots de passe depuis un appareil sain, déconnectez toutes les sessions, activez la MFA et supprimez le malware. Ne téléchargez pas de logiciels crackés ni de jeux piratés, source courante d'infostealers."),
      ("Ibyegeranyo by'amagambo y'ibanga, cookies, amakarita abitswe n'andi makuru infostealer ikoporora rwihishwa ku bikoresho byanduye, hanyuma abagizi ba nabi bakayacuruza cyangwa bakayasangiza.", "Niba igikoresho gishobora kuba cyaranduye, hindura amagambo y'ibanga ukoresheje igikoresho gisukuye, usohore sessions zose, ufungure MFA kandi ukureho malware. Ntuzakuremo porogaramu zacitswe cyangwa imikino y'ubusahuzi, isoko isanzwe ya infostealers."),
      ("Mafurushi ya nywila, cookies, kadi zilizohifadhiwa na data nyingine ambazo programu ya infostealer huiga kimya kimya kutoka vifaa vilivyoambukizwa, kisha wahalifu huuza au kushiriki.", "Kama kifaa kinaweza kuwa kimeambukizwa, badilisha nywila kutoka kifaa safi, toka kwenye vikao vyote, washa MFA na uondoe programu hasidi. Usipakue programu zilizovunjwa au michezo ya uharamia, chanzo cha kawaida cha infostealers.")),
    T("credential-reuse", "Credential reuse", ["credential reuse", "password reuse", "reusing passwords", "same password everywhere"], "identity", "keys on a ring", {"fr": "Réutilisation de mots de passe", "sw": "Kutumia nywila ileile", "rw": "Gukoresha ijambo ry'ibanga rimwe kuri konti nyinshi"},
      ("Using the same password on several accounts. If one site is breached, criminals try that email and password on banks, email and social media (credential stuffing).", "Use a different strong password for every account, kept in a password manager, and add MFA. Check whether your email appears in known breaches on a trusted breach-notification service."),
      ("Utiliser le même mot de passe sur plusieurs comptes. Si un site est piraté, les criminels essaient cet e-mail et ce mot de passe sur banques, messagerie et réseaux sociaux (credential stuffing).", "Utilisez un mot de passe fort différent pour chaque compte, rangé dans un gestionnaire de mots de passe, et ajoutez la MFA. Vérifiez si votre e-mail figure dans des fuites connues via un service de notification de fuites de confiance."),
      ("Gukoresha ijambo ry'ibanga rimwe kuri konti nyinshi. Urubuga rumwe nirumeneka, abagizi ba nabi bagerageza iyo imeri n'iryo jambo kuri banki, imeri n'imbuga nkoranyambaga (credential stuffing).", "Koresha ijambo ry'ibanga rikomeye rya buri konti, ribitswe muri password manager, wongereho MFA. Reba niba imeri yawe iri mu nyandiko zo kumeneka zizwi ukoresheje serivisi yizewe."),
      ("Kutumia nywila ileile kwenye akaunti nyingi. Tovuti moja ikidukuliwa, wahalifu hujaribu barua pepe na nywila hiyo kwenye benki, barua pepe na mitandao ya kijamii (credential stuffing).", "Tumia nywila imara tofauti kwa kila akaunti, iliyohifadhiwa kwenye kidhibiti cha nywila, na ongeza MFA. Angalia kama barua pepe yako iko kwenye uvujaji unaojulikana kupitia huduma ya kuaminika.")),
    T("data-leak-site", "Data leak site", ["data leak site", "leak site", "name and shame site", "ransomware leak site", "extortion site"], "attacks", "dark web website", {"fr": "Site de fuite de données", "sw": "Tovuti ya uvujaji wa data", "rw": "Urubuga rwo kumena amakuru"},
      ("A website where ransomware gangs publish or threaten to publish stolen data of victims who refuse to pay (double extortion).", "Victims should involve incident responders, legal advice and regulators, tell affected people and avoid relying on promises of deletion. Prevention (backups, patching, MFA, segmentation) matters more than negotiation."),
      ("Site où des groupes de rançongiciel publient ou menacent de publier les données volées de victimes qui refusent de payer (double extorsion).", "Les victimes doivent impliquer des équipes de réponse aux incidents, des conseils juridiques et les régulateurs, informer les personnes touchées et ne pas compter sur des promesses de suppression. La prévention (sauvegardes, correctifs, MFA, segmentation) compte plus que la négociation."),
      ("Urubuga aho udutsiko twa ransomware dutangaza cyangwa dutera ubwoba ko tuzatangaza amakuru yibwe y'abahohotewe banze kwishyura (double extortion).", "Abahohotewe bagomba gushyiramo abasubiza ibitero, inama z'amategeko n'abagenzuzi, kumenyesha abo bireba kandi ntibiringire ibyo bizeza byo gusiba. Kwirinda (backups, ivugurura, MFA, gutandukanya) bifite agaciro kurusha kuganira."),
      ("Tovuti ambapo magenge ya ransomware huchapisha au kutishia kuchapisha data iliyoibwa ya waathirika waliokataa kulipa (double extortion).", "Waathirika washirikishe wajibu wa matukio, ushauri wa kisheria na wasimamizi, wajulishe walioathirika na wasitegemee ahadi za kufuta. Kinga (nakala rudufu, viraka, MFA, kutenga) ni muhimu kuliko majadiliano.")),
    T("dark-web-marketplace", "Dark web marketplace", ["dark web marketplace", "darknet market", "darknet marketplace", "criminal marketplace", "underground forum"], "attacks", "hidden network", {"fr": "Marché du dark web", "sw": "Soko la dark web", "rw": "Isoko ryo kuri dark web"},
      ("Hidden websites and forums, reachable through special software such as Tor, where criminals buy and sell stolen data, malware, access to hacked networks and illegal goods.", "Defenders monitor such places for leaked company data (threat intelligence). Ordinary people should never buy there: it is illegal, scams between criminals are common, and visiting can expose you to malware."),
      ("Sites et forums cachés, accessibles par des logiciels spéciaux comme Tor, où des criminels achètent et vendent données volées, logiciels malveillants, accès à des réseaux piratés et biens illégaux.", "Les défenseurs y surveillent les fuites de données d'entreprise (renseignement sur les menaces). Les particuliers ne doivent jamais y acheter : c'est illégal, les arnaques entre criminels sont courantes et la visite expose aux malwares."),
      ("Imbuga n'amahuriro byihishe bigerwaho hakoreshejwe porogaramu yihariye nka Tor, aho abagizi ba nabi bagurisha bakanagura amakuru yibwe, malware, uburenganzira ku miyoboro yacitswe n'ibicuruzwa binyuranyije n'amategeko.", "Abarinzi bakurikirana ahantu nk'aho amakuru y'ibigo yamenetse (threat intelligence). Abantu basanzwe ntibagomba kuhagura: binyuranyije n'amategeko, uburiganya hagati y'abagizi ba nabi burasanzwe kandi kuhasura bishobora kukwanduza malware."),
      ("Tovuti na mabaraza yaliyofichwa, yanayofikiwa kwa programu maalum kama Tor, ambapo wahalifu hununua na kuuza data zilizoibwa, programu hasidi, ufikiaji wa mitandao iliyodukuliwa na bidhaa haramu.", "Walinzi hufuatilia maeneo kama hayo kwa uvujaji wa data za kampuni (threat intelligence). Watu wa kawaida wasinunue huko: ni kinyume cha sheria, ulaghai kati ya wahalifu ni wa kawaida na kutembelea kunaweza kukuweka hatarini kwa programu hasidi.")),
    T("bulletproof-hosting", "Bulletproof hosting", ["bulletproof hosting", "bulletproof host", "abuse-tolerant hosting"], "attacks", "data centre servers", {"fr": "Hébergement « bulletproof »", "sw": "Bulletproof hosting", "rw": "Bulletproof hosting"},
      ("Hosting services that deliberately ignore abuse complaints and takedown requests, so criminals can keep running phishing sites, malware servers and illegal shops.", "Defenders block or flag IP ranges known for abuse, share threat intelligence and work with registrars and hosts to take sites down. Report phishing sites to the hosting provider and to national incident teams."),
      ("Services d'hébergement qui ignorent volontairement les plaintes d'abus et demandes de retrait, permettant aux criminels de garder en ligne sites de phishing, serveurs de malwares et boutiques illégales.", "Les défenseurs bloquent ou signalent les plages d'IP connues pour abus, partagent le renseignement sur les menaces et travaillent avec registrars et hébergeurs pour retirer les sites. Signalez les sites de phishing à l'hébergeur et aux équipes nationales d'incident."),
      ("Serivisi zo kubika imbuga zirengagiza ku bushake ibirego by'ubugizi bwa nabi n'ibisabwa byo gukuraho, bigatuma abagizi ba nabi bakomeza kugira imbuga za phishing, seriveri za malware n'amaduka binyuranyije n'amategeko.", "Abarinzi bahagarika cyangwa bagaragaza IP zizwiho ubugizi bwa nabi, basangira threat intelligence kandi bakorana n'ababika imbuga ngo bazikureho. Menyesha imbuga za phishing utanga hosting n'amatsinda y'igihugu y'ibitero."),
      ("Huduma za hosting zinazopuuza kwa makusudi malalamiko ya matumizi mabaya na maombi ya kuondoa, ili wahalifu waendelee kuendesha tovuti za hadaa, seva za programu hasidi na maduka haramu.", "Walinzi huzuia au kuashiria safu za IP zinazojulikana kwa matumizi mabaya, hushiriki threat intelligence na kufanya kazi na wasajili na watoa hosting kuondoa tovuti. Ripoti tovuti za hadaa kwa mtoa hosting na timu za kitaifa za matukio.")),
    T("dark-patterns", "Dark patterns", ["dark patterns", "dark pattern", "deceptive design", "manipulative design", "trick interface"], "social", "confusing website buttons", {"fr": "Dark patterns (interfaces trompeuses)", "sw": "Dark patterns", "rw": "Dark patterns"},
      ("Interface designs that trick or pressure people into doing something they did not intend, such as hidden fees, pre-ticked boxes, fake countdown timers or buttons that make cancelling very hard.", "Slow down on checkout and sign-up pages, read what is pre-selected, check the final price and look for cancellation terms. Many data-protection and consumer laws treat deceptive consent designs as unfair."),
      ("Conceptions d'interface qui trompent ou poussent les gens à faire ce qu'ils ne voulaient pas : frais cachés, cases pré-cochées, faux comptes à rebours ou boutons rendant la résiliation très difficile.", "Ralentissez sur les pages de paiement et d'inscription, lisez ce qui est présélectionné, vérifiez le prix final et cherchez les conditions de résiliation. Beaucoup de lois sur les données et la consommation jugent déloyaux les consentements trompeurs."),
      ("Imiterere y'urubuga igamije kukuriganya cyangwa kugukanda ngo ukore ibyo utashakaga, nk'amafaranga ahishwe, udusanduku twatoranyijwe mbere, amasaha y'impimbano yo kubara cyangwa buto zituma guhagarika bigorana cyane.", "Genda gahoro ku mpapuro zo kwishyura no kwiyandikisha, soma ibyatoranyijwe mbere, reba igiciro cya nyuma kandi ushake amabwiriza yo guhagarika. Amategeko menshi y'amakuru n'abaguzi afata ibyemezo by'ubushutsi nk'ibidakwiye."),
      ("Miundo ya kiolesura inayodanganya au kushinikiza watu kufanya wasiyokusudia, kama ada zilizofichwa, visanduku vilivyochaguliwa awali, saa za kuhesabu za uongo au vitufe vinavyofanya kughairi kuwa vigumu.", "Punguza mwendo kwenye kurasa za malipo na kujisajili, soma kilichochaguliwa awali, angalia bei ya mwisho na tafuta masharti ya kughairi. Sheria nyingi za data na watumiaji huchukulia ridhaa za udanganyifu kuwa si za haki.")),
    T("spam", "Spam", ["spam", "junk mail", "unsolicited email", "unwanted messages", "spam email", "spam sms"], "social", "email junk folder", {"fr": "Spam (courrier indésirable)", "sw": "Barua taka (spam)", "rw": "Spam (ubutumwa budasabwe)"},
      ("Unwanted bulk messages (email, SMS, social media) sent to many people, used for advertising, scams and spreading malware.", "Do not reply, click or unsubscribe from suspicious spam (it confirms your address is real). Use spam filters, report and block, and never open attachments from unknown senders."),
      ("Messages de masse non sollicités (e-mail, SMS, réseaux sociaux) envoyés à beaucoup de gens, utilisés pour la publicité, les arnaques et la diffusion de logiciels malveillants.", "Ne répondez pas, ne cliquez pas et ne vous désabonnez pas d'un spam suspect (cela confirme que votre adresse est active). Utilisez les filtres anti-spam, signalez et bloquez, et n'ouvrez jamais les pièces jointes d'inconnus."),
      ("Ubutumwa bwinshi budasabwe (imeri, SMS, imbuga nkoranyambaga) bwoherezwa abantu benshi, bukoreshwa mu kwamamaza, uburiganya no gukwirakwiza malware.", "Ntusubize, ntukande cyangwa ngo wivane ku rutonde rwa spam ikekwa (bituma bamenya ko aderesi yawe ikora). Koresha spam filters, ubimenyeshe ubihagarike kandi ntuzigere ufungura attachments z'abo utazi."),
      ("Ujumbe mwingi usiohitajika (barua pepe, SMS, mitandao ya kijamii) unaotumwa kwa watu wengi, hutumika kwa matangazo, ulaghai na kusambaza programu hasidi.", "Usijibu, usibofye wala kujiondoa kwenye spam ya kutiliwa shaka (huthibitisha anwani yako ni halisi). Tumia vichujio vya spam, ripoti na uzuie, na kamwe usifungue viambatisho vya wasiojulikana.")),
    T("kyc-aml", "KYC and AML", ["kyc", "know your customer", "aml", "anti money laundering", "customer due diligence", "cdd"], "governance", "identity check at a bank", {"fr": "KYC et LCB-FT", "sw": "KYC na AML", "rw": "KYC na AML"},
      ("KYC (Know Your Customer) is verifying who a customer really is; AML (Anti-Money Laundering) is the set of rules and checks that stop dirty money from entering the financial system.", "It is why banks and mobile-money providers ask for ID. Criminals exploit this with fake “KYC update” messages: genuine providers update KYC in branches or inside the official app, never by asking for your PIN or a link."),
      ("KYC (Know Your Customer) consiste à vérifier qui est vraiment un client ; LCB-FT (AML) désigne les règles et contrôles qui empêchent l'argent sale d'entrer dans le système financier.", "C'est pourquoi banques et opérateurs mobile money demandent une pièce d'identité. Les criminels en abusent avec de faux messages de « mise à jour KYC » : les vrais opérateurs le font en agence ou dans l'application officielle, jamais en demandant votre PIN ou un lien."),
      ("KYC (Know Your Customer) ni ukugenzura uwo umukiriya ari we by'ukuri; AML (Anti-Money Laundering) ni amategeko n'igenzura bibuza amafaranga y'inyibano kwinjira mu rwego rw'imari.", "Ni yo mpamvu amabanki n'abatanga mobile money basaba indangamuntu. Abagizi ba nabi barabikoresha bohereza ubutumwa bw'impimbano «kuvugurura KYC»: abatanga serivisi nyabo babikorera mu mashami cyangwa muri porogaramu yemewe, ntibigera basaba PIN cyangwa link."),
      ("KYC (Know Your Customer) ni kuthibitisha mteja ni nani hasa; AML (Anti-Money Laundering) ni kanuni na ukaguzi vinavyozuia pesa chafu kuingia mfumo wa fedha.", "Ndiyo maana benki na watoa pesa za simu huomba kitambulisho. Wahalifu hutumia hili kwa ujumbe bandia wa «kusasisha KYC»: watoa huduma halisi hufanya hivyo matawini au kwenye programu rasmi, kamwe kwa kuomba PIN au kiungo.")),
]
